#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Shared pre-commit default: refuse a commit that stages an unparseable config file.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# 2026-08-24. A double hyphen inside an XML comment in
# idp/observability/clickhouse-low-memory.xml is illegal, so ClickHouse refused the
# whole file and crash-looped. langfuse-web and langfuse-worker wait on clickhouse
# being healthy, so neither was ever created, and docker ps -a showed them as
# Created, which reads as "not started yet" rather than "blocked upstream". Three
# hours. LAW 45 says the mistake is not closed until no session can walk past it.
#
# The primary guard is PreToolUse on Write and Edit, which catches every Claude
# session before the bytes land. This is the second layer, for the writes that never
# go through a Claude tool: a human editor, another vendor's CLI, a generated file.
#
# WHY NOT pre-commit (the framework)
# pre-commit's check-xml / check-yaml / check-json / check-toml (pre-commit-hooks
# v6.0.0) are the mature tools for this and would be the right answer on a normal
# machine. `pre-commit install` refuses to run when core.hooksPath is set, and every
# repository on this estate sets core.hooksPath to this directory so that one router
# serves them all. Installing the framework means giving that up in every repo. So
# this calls the estate's own checker, which is one implementation shared with the
# PreToolUse guard and the scheduled sweep -- three callers, one definition of
# "broken" (LAW 3).
#
# HOW IT FAILS
# Open. No python3, no checker, no staged files -> exit 0 and the commit proceeds.
# A gate that blocks every commit on this machine is a worse outage than the defect
# it prevents, and this router has already caused that once (see _router).
#
# THE ESCAPE
#   git commit --no-verify
set -uo pipefail

SWEEP="$HOME/.claude/scripts/config-syntax-sweep.py"
command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1 || exit 0
[ -f "$SWEEP" ] || exit 0

# Added, copied or modified files only. A deleted file has nothing to parse.
mapfile -t staged < <(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=ACM -z \
  | tr '\0' '\n' | grep -Ei '\.(xml|ya?ml|json|jsonc|toml)$' || true)
[ "${#staged[@]}" -gt 0 ] || exit 0

out="$(python3 "$SWEEP" --files "${staged[@]}" 2>&1)"
rc=$?
[ "$rc" -eq 0 ] && exit 0

echo "$out" >&2
cat >&2 <<'EOF'

REFUSED: a staged config file cannot be parsed by the service that reads it.
A service refuses the whole file at startup, and anything waiting on its health
is never created -- which reads as "not started yet", not as a fault.

Fix the syntax, or commit with --no-verify and say why.
EOF
exit 1
